    "text": "If the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfenced></math> defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is one-one and onto, then the distance of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> is:",
